### A · Measuring status

1. The **Global Gender Gap Index** of the World Economic Forum began in ==2006==.
2. Its four sub-indices are **economic participation, educational attainment, health and survival, and political empowerment**.
3. In ==2006== Pakistan ranked ==112th of 115==.
4. In ==2017== Pakistan ranked ==143rd of 144== — the "**second-worst**" country (2018 question).
5. Pakistan's rank in the Global Gender Gap Report 2023 was ==142nd of 146== (MCQ 2024).
6. In the **Global Gender Gap Report 2025** Pakistan ranked **last**, ==148th of 148==, with ==56.7%== of the gap closed.
7. In 2025 the share of women among Pakistan's federal **ministers** fell to **zero**.
8. In ==2026== Pakistan rose to ==143rd of 145==, with ==59.5%== of the gap closed.
9. In 2026 Pakistan ranked ==144th== on **economic participation**, ==130th== on **education** and ==107th== on **political empowerment**.
10. The global gender gap was ==69.2%== closed in 2026; parity is ==120 years== away; **Iceland** ranked first.
11. The UNDP's **Gender Inequality Index** began in ==2010==; the **Gender Development Index** in ==1995==.
12. The index measures **gaps**, not absolute well-being.

### B · Health

13. Pakistan's **maternal mortality ratio** was ==186== per 100,000 live births (**PMMS 2019**).
14. About ==42%== of women of reproductive age were **anaemic** (National Nutrition Survey 2018).
15. About ==40%== of children under five were **stunted** (NNS 2018).
16. The **total fertility rate** was about ==3.6== (PDHS 2017–18).
17. About ==34%== of married women used **contraception** (PDHS 2017–18).
18. About **two-thirds** of births were assisted by a skilled provider (PDHS 2017–18).
19. A 2019 paper stated that about **13,000** lives a year are lost in Pakistan to **breast cancer** (MCQ 2019).
20. The WHO defines health as complete physical, mental and social **well-being** (==1946==).
21. The **Lady Health Worker Programme** began in ==1994== under **Benazir Bhutto**.
22. The **Supreme Court** ordered the regularisation of Lady Health Workers in ==2012==.
23. The **Sehat Sahulat Programme** (health card) was launched in ==2015–16==.
24. Public spending on health has long been around **1% of GDP**.
25. After the **18th Amendment** (==2010==), health became a **provincial** subject.
26. Pakistan introduced the **HPV vaccine** for girls in ==2025==.

### C · Maternal health and Fathalla

27. **Mahmoud Fathalla**, an Egyptian obstetrician, described the "**road to maternal death**" (2024 question).
28. Fathalla asked "**Why did Mrs X die?**" at the **Safe Motherhood Conference**, **Nairobi**, ==1987==.
29. The Nairobi conference launched the global **Safe Motherhood Initiative** (==1987==).
30. Fathalla: women die not of untreatable diseases but because societies have not decided their **lives are worth saving**.
31. **Thaddeus and Maine** (==1994==) described the **three delays**: deciding, reaching and receiving care.
32. The main causes of maternal death are **haemorrhage, hypertension, infection, obstructed labour and unsafe abortion**.
33. **SDG target 3.1**: a global maternal mortality ratio below **70** by ==2030==.
34. Pakistan's population was about ==241 million== in the **Census 2023**, growing at about **2.55%** a year.
35. About ==650,000== pregnant women were in areas affected by the ==2022== floods (UNFPA).

### D · Education

36. **Article 25A** (18th Amendment, ==2010==) requires free and compulsory education for ages **5 to 16**.
37. The **Census 2023** literacy rate was ==60.65%== — about ==68%== for men and ==53%== for women.
38. The female literacy rate stated in a 2019 paper was ==48%== (MCQ 2019).
39. More than **25 million** children in Pakistan are out of school, most of them **girls**.
40. **Balochistan** has the lowest female literacy in Pakistan.
41. **Malala Yousafzai** was shot on ==9 October 2012== and won the Nobel Peace Prize in ==2014==.
42. Militants banned girls' education in **Swat** in ==2007==–==2009==.
43. **Punjab's female school stipend** (from 2004) raised girls' secondary enrolment.
44. The "**doctor brides**" phenomenon: many women medical graduates never practise.

### E · Employment

45. Female **labour-force participation** was ==24.4%== in the **LFS 2024–25** (21.4% in 2020–21).
46. Female LFPR by province: **Punjab** 33.8%, **KP** 21.1%, **Sindh** 20.5%, **Balochistan** 14.5%.
47. **Artificial unseen barriers** preventing career growth are called the **glass ceiling** (MCQ 2024).
48. The **sticky floor** refers to women stuck in **low-wage, low-mobility** jobs (MCQ 2026).
49. **Comparable-worth** discrimination refers to **sex segregation and less pay** for women's work (MCQ 2023).
50. **Arlie Hochschild** named the "**second shift**" (==1989==).
51. Women do about **three times** as much unpaid care work as men worldwide (ILO, ==2018==).
52. The **Protection against Harassment of Women at the Workplace Act** was passed in ==2010== (MCQs 2016, 2018, 2019, 2024).
53. The harassment law was **amended** in ==2022== to widen "workplace" and "employee".
54. A **10% quota** for women in federal services was given under the **PML-Q** in ==2002== (MCQ 2018 key).
55. **Sindh** passed the first **Home-Based Workers Act** in ==2018==.
56. **Punjab** passed a **Domestic Workers Act** in ==2019==.
57. The federal **Maternity and Paternity Leave Act** was passed in ==2020==.
58. **Justice Ayesha Malik** became the first woman judge of the **Supreme Court** in ==2022==.

### F · Constitution and family law

59. **Article 25**: no discrimination on the basis of **sex**; special provision for women allowed.
60. **Article 34**: **full participation of women** in all spheres of national life.
61. **Article 35**: protection of **marriage, family, mother and child**.
62. **Article 37(e)**: **maternity benefits** for women in employment.
63. **Article 32**: representation of **women** in local government.
64. The **Muslim Family Laws Ordinance** was enacted in ==1961== (MCQs 2016, 2018).
65. Under the MFLO, a second marriage needs the permission of an **Arbitration Council**.
66. Under the MFLO, a *talaq* takes effect **90 days** after notice to the Union Council.
67. The MFLO gave **orphaned grandchildren** a right to inherit.
68. The minimum age of girls for marriage under the old federal **Child Marriage Restraint Act** is **16** (MCQs 2016, 2019).
69. The **Sindh Child Marriages Restraint Act 2013** set the age at **18**.
70. The **ICT Child Marriage Restraint Act 2025** set **18** in Islamabad (assent ==30 May 2025==).
71. The **Punjab Assembly** passed a child-marriage restriction bill in ==April 2026==.
72. The **Federal Shariat Court** (==2021==) held a minimum marriage age is **not against Islam**.
73. The **Dissolution of Muslim Marriages Act** was passed in ==1939==.
74. ***Khurshid Bibi v. Muhammad Amin*** (==1967==) recognised a wife's right to ***khula***.
75. The **Saima Waheed** case (SC ==2004==) upheld an adult woman's right to marry **without a wali's consent**.
76. The **Family Courts Act** was passed in ==1964==.
77. The **Dowry and Bridal Gifts (Restriction) Act** was passed in ==1976==.
78. The **Sindh Hindu Marriage Act** (==2016==) and federal **Hindu Marriage Act** (==2017==) allowed Hindu marriages to be registered.

### G · Protective laws and institutions

79. The **Hudood Ordinances** were enacted in ==1979==.
80. The **Protection of Women (Criminal Laws Amendment) Act 2006** was passed under **Pervez Musharraf** (MCQ 2016).
81. The 2006 Act moved **rape** from the Zina Ordinance to the **Pakistan Penal Code**.
82. The **NCSW** was established in ==2000== under **Pervez Musharraf** (MCQ 2016).
83. The **National Policy for Development and Empowerment of Women** was launched in ==2002== (MCQ 2018).
84. The **Acid Control and Acid Crime Prevention Act** was passed in ==2011==.
85. The **Prevention of Anti-Women Practices Act 2011** criminalised forced marriage, ***vani*/*swara***, and denial of inheritance.
86. **Sindh** passed the first provincial **domestic violence** law in ==2013==.
87. The **anti-honour-killing** law of **October 2016** made **life imprisonment mandatory** even if the family forgives.
88. **Qandeel Baloch** was killed by her brother in **July** ==2016==.
89. The **Prevention of Electronic Crimes Act** was passed in ==2016==.
90. The **Enforcement of Women's Property Rights Act** (Islamabad) was passed in ==2020==.
91. The **Anti-Rape (Investigation and Trial) Act** of ==2021== created **special courts**.
92. The **National Commission for Human Rights** was created by the **NCHR Act 2012**.
93. The 2020 question's wording echoes the preamble of the **NCHR Act 2012**.
94. The first **violence-against-women centre** opened in **Multan** in ==2017==.
95. Punjab's women's helpline number is **1043**.
96. Pakistan ratified the **ICCPR** in ==2010== and the **ICESCR** in ==2008==.

### H · Intersectionality, digital and politics

97. **Intersectionality** was coined by **Kimberlé Crenshaw** in ==1989==.
98. **Patricia Hill Collins** (==1990==) described the **matrix of domination**.
99. Human-rights groups report **forced conversion and marriage** of Hindu and Christian girls, especially in **Sindh** and **Punjab**.
100. Pakistan ratified the **Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities** in ==2011==.
101. A job quota for persons with disabilities dates from the **Disabled Persons Ordinance 1981**.
102. The former tribal areas merged with **Khyber Pakhtunkhwa** in ==2018==.
103. Pakistan's **mobile-internet gender gap** fell from ==38%== to ==25%== (GSMA, 2024–25).
104. About **eight million** more women came online in Pakistan in 2024–25.
105. The **GSMA** publishes the annual *Mobile Gender Gap Report*.
106. A SIM card in Pakistan must be registered to a **CNIC**.
107. The **Digital Rights Foundation** runs a cyber-harassment helpline (from ==2016==).
108. **SDG target 5.b** calls for using **technology** to empower women.
109. The National Assembly has ==336== seats, including ==60== reserved for women.
110. Only ==11== women won **general** National Assembly seats in ==2024==.
111. **Maryam Nawaz** became the first woman **chief minister** (Punjab) in ==2024==.
112. **Benazir Bhutto** became prime minister in ==1988==; **Fahmida Mirza** the first woman Speaker in ==2008==.
113. The **Elections Act 2017** requires **5%** of tickets for women and allows voiding results where women's turnout is below **10%**.
114. The **Women's Parliamentary Caucus** was formed in ==2008==.
115. The **devolution plan** of ==2000–01== reserved **33%** of local seats for women.
116. Pakistan emits **less than 1%** of global greenhouse gases.
117. **Jacobabad** is regularly among the **hottest cities** on earth.
118. The **Benazir Income Support Programme** (==2008==) pays cash to **women**.
119. The biggest single gap in Pakistan's gender-gap score is **economic participation**.
120. The central weakness of Pakistan's women's laws is the **enforcement gap**.
